From: CEB-GNRD board layer <bmc@localhost>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] x86-power-control: do not share the Chassis.Buttons bus name

x86-power-control and phosphor-buttons both request the bus name
xyz.openbmc_project.Chassis.Buttons.  Whichever starts first owns it, and
when x86-power-control wins phosphor-buttons' objects (the UID button) are
never reachable, so phosphor-button-handler never sees the UID button and
the identify LED does not follow it.  Give the buttons exported by
x86-power-control a name of their own.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board specific: phosphor-buttons is used]
---
diff --git a/src/power_control.cpp b/src/power_control.cpp
--- a/src/power_control.cpp
+++ b/src/power_control.cpp
@@ -117,7 +117,9 @@
 static std::string hostDbusName = "xyz.openbmc_project.State.Host";
 static std::string chassisDbusName = "xyz.openbmc_project.State.Chassis";
 static std::string osDbusName = "xyz.openbmc_project.State.OperatingSystem";
-static std::string buttonDbusName = "xyz.openbmc_project.Chassis.Buttons";
+// phosphor-buttons owns xyz.openbmc_project.Chassis.Buttons on this board; two
+// daemons cannot share the name, so the buttons exported here get their own.
+static std::string buttonDbusName = "com.ctopai.CebGnrd.PowerControl.Buttons";
 static std::string nmiDbusName = "xyz.openbmc_project.Control.Host.NMI";
 static std::string rstCauseDbusName =
     "xyz.openbmc_project.Control.Host.RestartCause";
